Article 14 The functions of the Committee for Safeguarding National Security of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region shall be:
(1) to analyze and assess the situation concerning the safeguarding of national security in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, plan relevant work, and formulate policies on safeguarding national security in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region;
(2) to advance the establishment of the legal system and enforcement mechanisms for safeguarding national security in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region;
(3) to coordinate key work and major actions for safeguarding national security in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region.
The work of the Committee for Safeguarding National Security of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region shall not be subject to interference by any other institution, organization, or individual in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, and information relating to its work shall not be disclosed. Decisions made by the Committee for Safeguarding National Security of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region shall not be subject to judicial review.

Article 17 The functions of the department for safeguarding national security of the Hong Kong Police Force shall be:
(1) to collect and analyze intelligence and information concerning national security;
(2) to deploy, coordinate, and advance measures and actions for safeguarding national security;
(3) to investigate criminal cases that endanger national security;
(4) to conduct counter-interference investigations and carry out national security reviews;
(5) to undertake tasks relating to the safeguarding of national security assigned by the Committee for Safeguarding National Security of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region;
(6) to perform other functions necessary for the implementation of this Law.

Article 20 A person who organizes, plans, commits, or participates in any of the following acts aimed at secession of the State or subversion of national unity, whether or not by force or threat of force, commits an offence:
(1) secession of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region or any other part of the People's Republic of China from the People's Republic of China;
(2) unlawful alteration of the legal status of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region or any other part of the People's Republic of China;
(3) subjection of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region or any other part of the People's Republic of China to the domination of a foreign State.
A person who commits the offence in the preceding paragraph shall, if he is a principal or if the offence is of a grave nature, be sentenced to life imprisonment or fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years; if he actively participates, be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years; if he otherwise participates, be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years, criminal detention, or public surveillance.

Article 22 A person who organizes, plans, commits, or participates in any of the following acts by force, threat of force or other unlawful means aimed at subverting the State power commits an offence:
(1) overthrowing or undermining the fundamental system of the People's Republic of China as established by the Constitution of the People's Republic of China;
(2) overthrowing the Central People's Government of the People's Republic of China or the government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region;
(3) seriously interfering with, obstructing, or undermining the lawful exercise of functions by the Central People's Government of the People's Republic of China or the government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region;
(4) attacking or damaging the premises and facilities where the government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region exercises its functions, causing such premises and facilities to be unable to function normally.
A person who commits the offence in the preceding paragraph shall, if he is a principal or if the offence is of a grave nature, be sentenced to life imprisonment or fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years; if he actively participates, be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years; if he otherwise participates, be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years, criminal detention, or public surveillance.

Article 24 A person who, in order to coerce the Central People's Government, the Government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, or an international organization, or to intimidate the public in order to achieve political objectives, organizes, plans, commits, participates in, or threatens to commit any of the following terrorist activities that cause or are intended to cause serious social harm, commits an offence:
(1) serious violence against persons;
(2) explosion, arson, or dissemination of poisonous, radioactive, or infectious disease substances;
(3) sabotage of means of transport, transport facilities, electric power facilities, gas facilities, or other flammable or explosive equipment;
(4) serious interference with or disruption of electronic control systems for public services and management such as water, electricity, gas, transport, communications, and the internet;
(5) other dangerous acts that seriously endanger public health or safety.
A person who commits the offence in the preceding paragraph, if it causes serious injury, death, or heavy losses to public or private property, shall be sentenced to life imprisonment or fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years; in other cases, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years.

Article 29 A person who steals, spies on, buys or illegally provides State secrets or intelligence relating to national security for foreign or external institutions, organisations or individuals; or requests foreign or external institutions, organisations or individuals to commit, conspires with foreign or external institutions, organisations or individuals to commit, or directly or indirectly receives instructions, control, funding or other forms of support from foreign or external institutions, organisations or individuals to commit any of the following acts, commits an offence:
(1) launching a war against the People's Republic of China, or using force or threat of force to cause serious harm to the sovereignty, unification and territorial integrity of the People's Republic of China;
(2) seriously obstructing the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government or the Central People's Government in formulating and enforcing laws and policies, which may cause serious consequences;
(3) manipulating or undermining elections of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, which may cause serious consequences;
(4) imposing sanctions, blockade or taking other hostile actions against the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region or the People's Republic of China;
(5) provoking, through various illegal means, hatred by residents of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region against the Central People's Government or the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Government, which may cause serious consequences.
Whoever commits the offence set out in the preceding paragraph shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years; if the offence is grave, the person shall be sentenced to life imprisonment or fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years.
The foreign or external institutions, organisations or individuals involved in the acts set out in paragraph 1 of this Article shall be convicted and punished as joint offenders.

Article 33 Where any of the following circumstances exist, a lighter or mitigated punishment may be imposed on the offender, criminal suspect or defendant; if the crime is minor, the punishment may be exempted:
(1) the person voluntarily abandons the crime or voluntarily and effectively prevents the occurrence of the criminal result in the course of committing the crime;
(2) the person voluntarily surrenders and truthfully confesses their own crimes;
(3) the person reports others' criminal acts which are verified, or provides important clues that lead to the detection of other cases.
Where a criminal suspect or defendant who has been subjected to compulsory measures truthfully confesses other crimes specified in this Law committed by themselves that are not yet known to the law enforcement or judicial organs, the matter shall be handled in accordance with the provisions of item (2) of the preceding paragraph.

Article 43 When handling criminal cases endangering national security, the department for safeguarding national security of the Hong Kong Police Force of the Government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region may take the various measures that are permitted under the current laws of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region for the police and other law enforcement departments to take when investigating serious criminal cases, and may take the following measures:
(1) search premises, vehicles, ships, aircraft, and other relevant places and electronic devices that may contain evidence of a crime;
(2) require any person suspected of committing an act endangering national security to surrender travel documents or restrict the person from leaving the territory;
(3) freeze property used or intended for criminal purposes, proceeds of crime, and other property related to crime, and apply for a restriction order, charging order, order for forfeiture, or confiscation order;
(4) require any person disseminating information or relevant service provider to remove information or provide assistance;
(5) require political organizations from foreign or external sources, or agents of foreign or external authorities or political organizations to provide information;
(6) subject to the approval of the Chief Executive, intercept communications and conduct covert surveillance on persons reasonably suspected of being involved in committing a crime endangering national security;
(7) require any person reasonably suspected of possessing information related to the investigation or having custody of relevant materials to answer questions and produce information or materials.
The Committee for Safeguarding National Security of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region shall have the supervisory responsibility over the law enforcement bodies, including the department for safeguarding national security of the Hong Kong Police Force, when they take the measures specified in the first paragraph of this Article.
The Chief Executive of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region is authorized, jointly with the Committee for Safeguarding National Security of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, to formulate relevant detailed implementation rules for taking the measures specified in the first paragraph of this Article.

Article 49 The duties of the Office for Safeguarding National Security in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region are:
(1) to analyze and assess the national security situation in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, and to make recommendations and suggestions on major strategies and important policies for safeguarding national security;
(2) to oversee, guide, coordinate, and support the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region in performing its duties for safeguarding national security;
(3) to collect and analyze intelligence information on national security; and
(4) to handle criminal cases endangering national security according to law.
